    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ablēgātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		ablego, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a sending off</i> or <i>away</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juventutis ad bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					6, 39, 7</span></i>
			.—A euphemism for <i>banishing</i>,
				<i>exile</i> (= relegatio): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Agrippae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 45, 46, § 149</span></i>
			.</div>
